508:We consider $j$ as a potential candidate node -- and move up towards the root -- only when the previous two conditions are not satisfied (Line 11-12). Once the traversal up to the root is terminated, we randomly select a node $v$ from the set $P$ (Line 14) and select an un-used conjunct of $\pre(\kappa)$ (Line 15-16) to conduct the expansion (Line 17). Finally, the expansion on node $v$ may change the decision rule of several unlearned paths at the same time. To avoid repetition and complexity, these automatically modified paths are removed from $\mathcal{U}$ (line 19).
