226:In this paper, we consider a generic form of  knowledge $\kappa$, which is of the form as in Eq.~\eqref{equ:knowledgeexpression}. First, we show that $\kappa$ can express backdoor attacks. In a backdoor attack, an adversary (e.g., an operator who trains machine learning models, or an attacker who is able to modify the model) embeds malicious \textit{knowledge about triggers} into the machine learning model, requiring that for any input with the given trigger, the model will return a specific target label. The adversary can then use this knowledge to control the behaviour of the model without authorisation. 
