\subsection{Knowledge Extraction}\label{defence}

For the extraction of embedded knowledge, we use a set of (50 normal and 50 KE) samples and apply activation pattern based outlier detection method %(see Appendix \ref{sec:defencebyoutlier}) 
to compute the set $\Sigma'(M,y)$ of suspected joint paths. Then, SMT solver is used to compute Eq.~\eqref{equ:l0_norm} with $\Sigma'(M,y)$ and the training dataset as inputs for the set $\mathcal{D}'$. Only $m = 3$ features are allowed to be changed. Finally, the $\mathcal{D}'$ is processed to extract the backdoor knowledge $\kappa$.

