codex
Implemented a provisional Track B problem generator based on the paper’s Section 6, Theorem 1 reduction. The family inverse-generates affine-XOR constraints, compiles them into Boolean decision-tree ensembles, and checks witnesses through exact tree evaluation and majority voting. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.08281)

Deliverables:

- [gen_2010_08281.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/gen_2010_08281.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All nine deterministic gates pass.
- Shipping preset: 127 features and 2,540 clause trees.
- Exact rank: 120; exactly 128 valid witnesses among \(2^{127}\), density \(2^{-120}\).
- Four adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference GF(2) elimination: 8/8, averaging 1,140,137 counted bit operations.
- Strengthened canonicalization passed 100/100 symmetry checks.
- Answer: 129 serialized characters; compact route: 120 XORs.

The result is not fully hardened: every OpenRouter request returned HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded,” so STEP 4 has no valid oracle attempts. The repository validator therefore blocks submission solely on the missing multi-vendor evidence. The error transcripts are preserved and are explicitly not represented as model failures. No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an external quota blockage, not a G/H/V rejection.
