codex
The revised renderer now preserves every decision-tree vote while grouping only semantically identical three-feature supports; the hard instance is 635 readable four-tree blocks rather than 2,540 scattered rows. The compact method is now honestly budgeted at 240 binary XORs. I also added a plain DPLL/unit-propagation reference: on shipping instances it succeeds in eight search nodes but still requires roughly 66,000 clause scans per instance, while the polynomial XOR solver uses about 1.14 million scalar bit operations.
