codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator grounded in the paper’s Theorem 1 tree-ensemble reduction ([paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.08281)).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/gen_2010_08281.py:1)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/README.md)
- [Hardening transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted G9 transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo G9 transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.08281/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All deterministic gates pass:

- Exact valid-answer density: \(2^{-120}\)
- Random guesses: 0/200,000
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each
- DPLL reference: 65,873 clause scans per instance
- Polynomial GF(2) reference: 1,140,137 scalar bit operations
- Compact route: 240 XORs
- Answer: 129 characters, 127 atoms
- Additional randomized verification: 800 instances and 30 exact enumerations

The required oracle evidence remains unavailable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded” for every main and G9 retry. Those errors are retained as script-generated transcripts and were not counted as model failures. Consequently, the module is locally verified but must not be submitted as fully hardened until the OpenRouter quota is restored and the four-vendor runs complete.
