README.md:22:Generation is inverse. The generator first samples a quadratic Boolean form $q$ and a linear form $\ell$ on the nonzero vectors of $\mathbb F_2^d$. It retains the input $q(v)\oplus\ell(v)$, creates identities on triples $(u,v,u\oplus v)$, compiles each identity into four 3-CNF clause trees, and shuffles feature and tree order. The certificate is known before the forest exists. `render` groups trees with the same three tested features and canonicalizes only their display order; every parenthesized tree remains a separate vote.
